==Russian==

===Etymology===
{{af|ru|по-|стоя́ть}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA|постоя́ть}}
* {{audio|ru|Ru-постоять.ogg}}

===Verb===
{{ru-verb|постоя́ть|pf|impf=стоя́ть}}

# to [[stand]] ''(for a while)''
#* {{quote-book|ru|year=1930|author=w:ru:Нина Берберова<t:{{w|Nina Berberova}}>|title=Последние и первые|chapter=VI|location=Paris|publisher=Jacques Povolozky & Cie|newversion=English translation from|translator2=w:Marian Schwartz|title2=The Last and the First|location2=London|publisher2=w:Pushkin Press|year2=2021|page2=|pageurl2=
|text=Она́ вбежа́ла наве́рх, с мину́ту '''постоя́ла''' на площа́дке, послу́шала, как Илья́ вошёл в но́мер.|t=She ran upstairs and '''stood''' on the landing for a minute, listening for Ilya to go into his room.}}
# to [[stand up for|stand up]] {{+obj|ru|:за(acc)<for someone>}}
#: {{coi|ru|'''постоя́ть''' [[за]] [[себя́]]|to [[stand up for]] oneself, to [[stick up for]] oneself}}
# {{lb|ru|in the imperative}} {{n-g|expresses a demand to [[stop]] or stop [[moving]]}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[значит|Зна́чит]], '''посто́й''', [[ты]] [[говори́шь]], [[что]]...|t=So, '''wait''', you're saying that...}}

